.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_KDF-SSHKDF 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_KDF-SSHKDF
.Nd The SSHKDF EVP_KDF implementation
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Support for computing the
.Sy SSHKDF
KDF through the
.Sy EVP_KDF
API.
.Pp
The EVP_KDF-SSHKDF algorithm implements the SSHKDF key derivation
function.
It is defined in RFC 4253, section 7.2 and is used by SSH to derive IVs,
encryption keys and integrity keys.
Five inputs are required to perform key derivation: The hashing function
(for example SHA256), the Initial Key, the Exchange Hash, the Session
ID, and the derivation key type.
.Pp
The output is considered to be keying material.
.Ss Identity
"SSHKDF" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_KDF_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
The supported parameters are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqproperties" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_PROPERTIES Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqdigest" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_DIGEST Ns ) <UTF8 string>
.It \(dqkey" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY Ns ) <octet string>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_KDF 3 .
.It \(dqxcghash" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SSHKDF_XCGHASH Ns ) <octet string>
.It \(dqsession_id" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SSHKDF_SESSION_ID Ns ) <octet string>
These parameters set the respective values for the KDF. If a value is
already set, the contents are replaced.
.It \(dqtype" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SSHKDF_TYPE Ns ) <UTF8 string>
This parameter sets the type for the SSHKDF operation.
There are six supported types:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It EVP_KDF_SSHKDF_TYPE_INITIAL_IV_CLI_TO_SRV
The Initial IV from client to server.
A single char of value 65 (ASCII char 'A').
.It EVP_KDF_SSHKDF_TYPE_INITIAL_IV_SRV_TO_CLI
The Initial IV from server to client A single char of value 66 (ASCII
char 'B').
.It EVP_KDF_SSHKDF_TYPE_ENCRYPTION_KEY_CLI_TO_SRV
The Encryption Key from client to server A single char of value 67
(ASCII char 'C').
.It EVP_KDF_SSHKDF_TYPE_ENCRYPTION_KEY_SRV_TO_CLI
The Encryption Key from server to client A single char of value 68
(ASCII char 'D').
.It EVP_KDF_SSHKDF_TYPE_INTEGRITY_KEY_CLI_TO_SRV
The Integrity Key from client to server A single char of value 69 (ASCII
char 'E').
.It EVP_KDF_SSHKDF_TYPE_INTEGRITY_KEY_SRV_TO_CLI
The Integrity Key from client to server A single char of value 70 (ASCII
char 'F').
.El
.El
.Pp
The OpenSSL FIPS provider also supports the following parameters:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
A getter that returns 1 if the operation is FIPS approved, or 0
otherwise.
This may be used after calling EVP_KDF_derive.
It returns 0 if any "***-check" related parameter is set to 0 and the
check fails.
.It \(dqdigest-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_DIGEST_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
The default value of 1 causes an error during
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
if used digest is not approved.
Setting this to zero will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.Pp
According to SP 800-135r1, the following are approved digest algorithms:
SHA-1, SHA2-224, SHA2-256, SHA2-384, SHA2-512.
.It \(dqkey-check" ( Ns Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_FIPS_KEY_CHECK Ns ) <integer>
The default value of 1 causes an error during
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_set_params 3
if the length of used key-derivation key
.Pf ( Sy OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY )
is shorter than 112 bits.
Setting this to zero will ignore the error and set the approved
"fips-indicator" to 0. This option breaks FIPS compliance if it causes
the approved "fips-indicator" to return 0.
.El
.Sh NOTES
A context for SSHKDF can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_KDF *kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "SSHKDF", NULL);
 EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
.Ed
.Pp
The output length of the SSHKDF derivation is specified via the
.Em keylen
parameter to the
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
function.
Since the SSHKDF output length is variable, calling
.Xr EVP_KDF_CTX_get_kdf_size 3
to obtain the requisite length is not meaningful.
The caller must allocate a buffer of the desired length, and pass that
buffer to the
.Xr EVP_KDF_derive 3
function along with the desired length.
.Sh EXAMPLES
This example derives an 8 byte IV using SHA-256 with a 1K "key" and
appropriate "xcghash" and "session_id" values:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_KDF *kdf;
 EVP_KDF_CTX *kctx;
 char type = EVP_KDF_SSHKDF_TYPE_INITIAL_IV_CLI_TO_SRV;
 unsigned char key[1024] = "01234...";
 unsigned char xcghash[32] = "012345...";
 unsigned char session_id[32] = "012345...";
 unsigned char out[8];
 size_t outlen = sizeof(out);
 OSSL_PARAM params[6], *p = params;

 kdf = EVP_KDF_fetch(NULL, "SSHKDF", NULL);
 kctx = EVP_KDF_CTX_new(kdf);
 EVP_KDF_free(kdf);

 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_DIGEST,
                                         SN_sha256, strlen(SN_sha256));
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_KEY,
                                          key, (size_t)1024);
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SSHKDF_XCGHASH,
                                          xcghash, (size_t)32);
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_octet_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SSHKDF_SESSION_ID,
                                          session_id, (size_t)32);
 *p++ = OSSL_PARAM_construct_utf8_string(OSSL_KDF_PARAM_SSHKDF_TYPE,
                                         &type, sizeof(type));
 *p = OSSL_PARAM_construct_end();
 if (EVP_KDF_derive(kctx, out, outlen, params) <= 0)
     /* Error */
.Ed
.Sh CONFORMING TO
RFC 4253
.Sh SEE ALSO
